{
  "id": "Compound::DB00119 - Gene::9123",
  "verbalization": "Pyruvic Acid is implicated in the interaction with Slc16a3 through a series of molecular pathways that involve the proton-coupled monocarboxylate transport system. The evidence suggests that Pyruvic Acid binds to Slc16a8 or Slc16a7, which are both involved in the transport of monocarboxylates across cellular membranes. These transporters, in turn, are part of the broader Lactate Transmembrane Transporter Activity, which is also associated with Slc16a3. This indicates a potential role for Pyruvic Acid in modulating the activity of Slc16a3 through its interaction with these transporters. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Pyruvic Acid and Slc16a3, particularly through the regulation of monocarboxylate transport. The observed scores suggest a consistent and significant interaction, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of this relationship.",
